#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# lucas_l

#% text
# `lucas_l(n)` gives the Lucas number L_n.

#% text
# `lucas_l(n, x)` gives the Lucas polynomial L_n(x).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# L_0 = 2, L_1 = 1, L_(n+1) = L_n + L_(n-1); L_n = F_(n-1) + F_(n+1).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
lucas_l(10)
#% output
#= 123

#% cell
lucas_l(4, x)
#% output
#= 2 + 4*x^2 + x^4

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
lucas_l(2.5)
#% output
#= 3.330190676785562

